From 7ab24dd738e6de5a3897ac75e40eb1f18f115d0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:28:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phase3-audit: fixture honesty + exec/demo dedup (B-3
 completion, D-3 completion)

The phase-2 audit's B-3 fix made SpawnClash dictionary-keyed; phase 3
then re-introduced raw EDU row indices in every NEW fixture surface:
RangedSpawnVolley (2/0), RangedPerfStress (2), the soak's archer mix
(Min(2, ...)), CombatPerfStress (0, pre-existing), and -- worst -- the
demo visuals' AdoptUnknownRegistryUnits keyed the demo FACTION on
EduRowIndex == 0. All now resolve rows by dictionary name through one
public helper (BattleExec::FindEduRowIndexByDictionary, promoted from
SpawnClash's file-local copy); the demo adopt reads the SIDE (TeamId),
and ADemoUnitActor syncs TeamId from its demo faction so an author's
visual faction and the sim's friend/enemy split cannot disagree.

Same file: LoadGoldenEduRows owns the fixture path+load+parse (was
re-typed 6x in the exec file + once in the demo); EnableRangedPipeline
owns the 4-cvar ranged session-on list (was re-typed in both ranged
fixtures); DemoGameMode's FindRow lambda (the third re-typed dictionary
matcher) is deleted.

MUST re-run on the UE machine: full unit + func tier (fixture paths
touched); Battle.Ranged.SpawnVolley/PerfStress + one SoakVolley nightly
(evidence lines unchanged in shape); PIE on the demo map (adopt-path
tinting is the only behavior-visible change: units spawned via exec
fixtures now tint by their TeamId).
